{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Harness built in experiment worktree (frontier-exp; throwaway, gitignored, not pushed). Executor-seam capture: the runner binds plain-function tools at run time (runner.py:333-341), so the harness wraps the module attributes rebar.llm.pai_tools.filesystem_tools (read_file/list_directory/search_files), pai_tools.grounding_tools (resolve_symbol), and pai_tools.rebar_tools (show_ticket; allow_comment FORCED False so every run is strictly read-only even in local mode), plus rebar.llm.workflow.completion_recovery.make_completion_record_tool (import-time binding, patch-where-used) to log record_criterion_verdict calls as criterion boundaries. Also patched: verify_step_floor at BOTH bindings (rebar.llm.completion + rebar.llm.workflow.completion_banking) to a flat 16 steps; completion_verdict_cache.cache_dir to per-(ticket,arm) dirs under experiment/caches; STEP_REGISTRY['completion_precheck'] wrapped to splice the data-shaped frontier block inside the <untrusted_ticket_context> fence (treatment arm only). Corpus: barky-metalled-bettong (45c1-513b-d97a-46d3, 7998 desc chars, 6 ACs, 15 file_impact) and deadbeat-warlike-ostrich (8d74-2c9f-c98f-4f0b, 7826 chars, 4 ACs). Runs: rebar.llm.completion.verify_completion(source='local', fetch=False), never signs. Launching now: 1 forced-exhaustion + up to 3 resume attempts per arm per ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786808363981255001,"uuid":"ff55cc8c-ff38-4b21-8fd2-a68d1195a07d"}